`attrs->GetAttrPointer<bool>(ATTR_IS_TRANS_B_INDEX)` is directly dereferenced without checking if the returned pointer is `nullptr`. If the attribute is missing or fails to retrieve, this will cause a segmentation fault.

```c
    auto isTransBPtr = attrs->GetAttrPointer<bool>(ATTR_IS_TRANS_B_INDEX);
    OPS_ERR_IF(isTransBPtr == nullptr,
        OPS_LOG_E(nodeName, "is_trans_b attribute is null."), return ge::GRAPH_FAILED);
    bool isTransB = *isTransBPtr;
```

